_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twalker1998/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-10T19:55:48Z","updated_at":"2023-11-10T20:08:52Z","body":"I'm still experiencing this on `13.5.6`. I'm not quite ready to upgrade to NextJS 14- perhaps it is fixed there? Either way, this bug still exists and I'd really like to not have to revert to an older version.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Downgrading to `13.2.3` isn't even an option for me, as my application depends on `useParams` [which wasn't introduced until `13.3.0`](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/functions/use-params#version-history).\r\n\r\n@leerob could we possibly get some attention on this issue? I understand you and your team have bigger fish to fry, but this is a pretty big problem. In the meantime, I'll be directing my users to refresh the page (which is a sufficient workaround), but that's not a good long term solution in my opinion. I'm happy to share my code and point out the routes where I'm experiencing this issue, if that would be helpful.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1806356125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"twalker1998","id":22465068,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlc